WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.560
- [Kris] The CEO of Vayner Media.

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.150
He's got a YouTube show,

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.200
written five best sellers,

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.250
Fortune Magazine 40 under 40.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.090
He is amazing.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:11.470
He's in studio.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:12.469
His name is Gary Vee.

00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:13.493
- Yo.

00:00:13.493 --> 00:00:14.326
(cheering)

00:00:14.326 --> 00:00:15.492
Love it.

00:00:15.492 --> 00:00:16.553
- [Kris] Welcome to Virgin Radio.

00:00:16.553 --> 00:00:17.500
Welcome to the Kris Fade Show.
- Thank you.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.720
- [Kris] What did you put your
money into back in the day

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.861
that people were like what
are you doing and now...

00:00:21.861 --> 00:00:26.370
- So back in 2007, I
put almost all my money

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.560
into Facebook and Twitter
and my financial advisors

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.799
and all the old liquor store guys I knew,

00:00:31.799 --> 00:00:33.890
people were just ridiculing me.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:34.723
- [Kris] Why?

00:00:34.723 --> 00:00:36.259
- Well they thought everything was a fad.

00:00:36.259 --> 00:00:39.279
My whole career, everything I've done

00:00:39.279 --> 00:00:41.380
people have been telling me is a fad.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:45.190
When I launched an
ecommerce wine site in 1996,

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:46.710
the internet was a fad.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.960
When I started running Google
ads instead of newspaper

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.210
and direct mail, Google was a fad.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.770
When I started my YouTube
show, YouTube was a fad.

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:56.947
When I invested in Facebook
and Twitter, that was a fad.

00:00:56.947 --> 00:01:00.700
Everything that I do tends to be a fad

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.260
or isn't gonna happen.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:05.990
Usually when most
conservative or people above

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:08.990
or older or successful
than me say something

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:10.260
I'm doing is a fad,

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.190
I've come to learn that's
when I need to triple down.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:13.383
(laughing)

00:01:13.383 --> 00:01:14.216
- [Kris] Okay I get that.

00:01:14.216 --> 00:01:15.410
It makes sense.

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:17.089
There's a couple things I
wanna play for you right now.

00:01:17.089 --> 00:01:22.089
Number one, were you aware
that there is a Filipino star

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:23.380
called Gary V?

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:24.401
- Very much.

00:01:24.401 --> 00:01:26.480
(laughing)

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.723
- [Kris] Kyle, can you come up?

00:01:27.723 --> 00:01:29.670
Kyle, you're Filipino, Kyle.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:30.640
Kyle, because...

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:31.473
- He's huge.

00:01:31.473 --> 00:01:33.477
- [Kris] I said in studio
the other day, I said,

00:01:33.477 --> 00:01:35.743
"Oh my gosh, we've got Gary V coming in."

00:01:35.743 --> 00:01:39.697
One of our presenters, Jay
Scar, who's Filipino says,

00:01:39.697 --> 00:01:42.517
"Oh my gosh! Gary
Valenciano is coming in?"

00:01:42.517 --> 00:01:43.350
- [Woman] She was so excited.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:44.737
- [Kris] And I went, "Who?"

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.820
He's a huge Filipino pop star.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:47.977
He's this guy...

00:01:47.977 --> 00:01:48.810
- He's very big.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:51.510
Even when I showed my
friend who's Gary V is,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:52.610
I said Google him.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.210
So Gary Valenciano comes up on Google.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.999
- I know, I saw his face.

00:01:55.999 --> 00:02:00.999
When I first started having
internet kind of notoriety,

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.750
a lot of people...

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:04.110
I mean, he would always show up.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:05.690
It would always be brought up.

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:07.729
I think I've done a good
job in the last five years.

00:02:07.729 --> 00:02:09.789
I've closed the gap.

00:02:09.789 --> 00:02:11.150
I've closed the gap.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:12.120
I have a lot of respect for him.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.460
I've listened to too much of his songs.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:16.495
- [Kris] We've got him on the
phone right now, no we don't.

00:02:16.495 --> 00:02:17.716
(laughing)

00:02:17.716 --> 00:02:19.577
- I was hoping.

00:02:19.577 --> 00:02:21.460
- [Kris] There's something
else that I wanted to...

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.190
We're talking about our kids.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.487
You're a family man as well.
- Yes.

00:02:24.487 --> 00:02:27.620
- [Kris] Just real quickly
again, I want that advice.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.040
Juggling the family and
the business and the life.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:30.873
How hard is that?

00:02:30.873 --> 00:02:32.310
How do you make it easier?

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:33.560
Is there a way?

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.440
- I think it's actually stunningly easy

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:37.300
as long as you don't succumb

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.720
to other people's opinions
on how you should parent

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.245
your children or the current state

00:02:41.245 --> 00:02:43.100
of what's politically correct.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.317
It gets very easy.

00:02:44.317 --> 00:02:46.477
Parenting comes very easy to me.

00:02:46.477 --> 00:02:49.970
I have great intent but for example,

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:52.734
there's a big Thanksgiving kind of recital

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:55.080
in the morning for my kids this week.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.473
I'm gonna miss it 'cause I'm here.

00:02:56.473 --> 00:03:00.310
I'm not happy about it
but I'm not crushed.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:02.910
I'm not gonna judge myself
like I'm the worst dad

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:03.770
of all time.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:05.667
Showing your kids how to live happy

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:08.900
is the number one thing you
can do for your children.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:09.733
- [Interviewer] 'Cause your mother

00:03:09.733 --> 00:03:12.500
was very influential in that
factor when you were younger.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:13.333
- Huge.

00:03:13.333 --> 00:03:17.410
But my dad worked every minute
'cause we were immigrants.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.060
He never came to anything I did

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:21.760
and very honestly my mom didn't
go to school stuff either.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.240
She was kind of like an immigrant lady.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:24.385
She was to herself.

00:03:24.385 --> 00:03:28.160
Basically for me it's very binary.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.920
Do your parents love you
and put you in a position

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:31.900
to be happy?

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:35.003
Everything else is checking
the box for everybody else.

00:03:35.996 --> 00:03:38.010
- [Kris] Talking about my kids.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:39.900
This is what I've got right now for you.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.470
I've got my girls, Noushie and Kikki

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:42.611
doing some of your...

00:03:42.611 --> 00:03:44.072
Have a listen to this.

00:03:44.072 --> 00:03:45.252
(laughing)

00:03:45.252 --> 00:03:46.292
Have a listen to this.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.293
Here we go.

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.800
Gary V read by Noushie
and Kikki, my daughters.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.334
- [Daughter] Let me tell you...

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:51.375
(laughing)

00:03:51.375 --> 00:03:56.314
I believe one of the most
fascinating excuses in life is

00:03:56.314 --> 00:03:58.574
I'm so good at so many things

00:03:58.574 --> 00:04:00.074
that I don't know which one to pick.

00:04:00.074 --> 00:04:01.073
- She's right.

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:01.930
- [Daughter] I think it's an excuse

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:03.529
and I think it's ego.

00:04:03.529 --> 00:04:05.530
I think it's a vulnerability.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.230
(laughing)

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:09.640
I don't wanna waste my time

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.905
'cause I'm so good at many things.

00:04:11.905 --> 00:04:13.065
- So good.

00:04:13.065 --> 00:04:14.146
- It's an excuse to not do.
- Truth.

00:04:14.146 --> 00:04:15.266
- [Daughter] And it's the worst one

00:04:15.266 --> 00:04:16.446
'cause you're trying to act cool

00:04:16.446 --> 00:04:19.466
while not doing anything.

00:04:19.466 --> 00:04:22.318
Pick something and (censored) do it.

00:04:22.318 --> 00:04:25.000
(laughing)

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.570
- [Kris] These are your words.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:27.403
- It's amazing.

00:04:27.403 --> 00:04:28.480
- [Kris] And that's a big one,

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.083
worrying about other people's opinions.

00:04:30.083 --> 00:04:31.561
- It's huge.

00:04:31.561 --> 00:04:32.394
- [Kris] You always hit that one

00:04:32.394 --> 00:04:33.890
and that's a big thing, right?

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:36.070
- After doing this for
about seven or eight years

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:38.200
where you're getting 1,000 comments back

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.730
in email, DM, whatever it may be

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:43.270
it took me a long time
but I'm like, oh my god,

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:45.640
it's judgment, it's
other people's opinions.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.480
It was so foreign to me
'cause I was in such a cocoon.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.442
I never listened...

00:04:50.442 --> 00:04:52.870
So many things that kept
me away from bad things

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:55.770
as a teenager was I was in my own head.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.856
Nobody else's opinion penetrated me

00:04:57.856 --> 00:05:00.810
which didn't lead me to those actions.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.140
So it was foreign to me to realize

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:05.711
oh my god, the rest of the
world lives a different way.

00:05:05.711 --> 00:05:08.930
And that is why I'm
trying to suffocate that

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:12.280
because the more I can
get people into a place

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:15.670
of feeling confident about
themselves for themselves,

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:19.132
it's unbelievable what
happens when you can actually

00:05:19.132 --> 00:05:22.020
cut out the noise of judgment of others.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.550
It's a big deal.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.950
And honestly, and it's
fun to be in this region

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:28.480
because it's a phenomenon outside the US,

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:30.000
even though it's big in the US.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.680
It's parents.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.520
The amount of people right
now who are listening

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.744
who are living their lives 100%

00:05:35.744 --> 00:05:38.750
based on their parents'
opinions is staggering.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:40.710
Now, let me create some clarity.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:42.960
If you want your parents
to pay for your lifestyle,

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:43.910
well guess what?

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.021
Then they own you.

00:05:45.021 --> 00:05:49.010
But if you don't and you wanna be happy

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:50.230
and you don't wanna be an engineer

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:52.697
or a doctor or an entrepreneur
or whatever it may be,

00:05:52.697 --> 00:05:55.320
you first have to get off the payroll,

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:57.960
be a big boy and girl
and then you have to do.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.590
You may have some short term pain

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:00.816
where your parents are disappointed

00:06:00.816 --> 00:06:04.610
but long term you'll have a
far healthier relationship

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:06.130
because the only thing
your parents usually

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:09.370
are worried about unfortunately
is the judgment of others.

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:10.770
- [Woman] What are they gonna think?

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:14.028
- It's your aunt that is the hidden issue.

00:06:14.028 --> 00:06:17.050
'Cause your mom's trying
to make you a lawyer

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:19.960
because she wants her sister
to think you're successful.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:23.761
It's a very complicated
mindset but it's the truth.

00:06:23.761 --> 00:06:26.820
- [Kris] Talking to you
when the mics are off

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:28.080
is even more interesting.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:28.960
(laughing)

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:29.793
He doesn't stop.

00:06:29.793 --> 00:06:31.240
- [Woman] No.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:32.073
- [Kris] You get people coming in.

00:06:32.073 --> 00:06:33.614
You get artists and
superstars and all to come in

00:06:33.614 --> 00:06:35.410
and they turn it on when the mic's on.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.243
- Interesting.

00:06:36.243 --> 00:06:37.480
- [Kris] And when the
mic's off, they're off.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:38.695
- Interesting.

00:06:38.695 --> 00:06:39.528
- [Kris] They just sit there and you're on

00:06:39.528 --> 00:06:41.556
and you're just, I love that.

00:06:41.556 --> 00:06:45.010
- And honestly I have empathy for people

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:45.880
that need to shut it off.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.075
For me, this is like the most fun.

00:06:48.075 --> 00:06:52.635
Social media, the timing of
my life is laughable to me.

00:06:52.635 --> 00:06:55.054
To me I love people so much,

00:06:55.054 --> 00:06:57.840
interacting with people is my oxygen.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:00.470
- Yeah, but you were
asking about us as people.

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:02.452
You were asking about how we started.

00:07:02.452 --> 00:07:04.923
Not many people do that when
they come into the studio.

00:07:04.923 --> 00:07:06.353
- [Woman] It's a human connection.

00:07:06.353 --> 00:07:07.372
- It's a human connection.

00:07:07.372 --> 00:07:08.393
- Well it's funny.

00:07:08.393 --> 00:07:09.226
Social media is so
powerful which you're on

00:07:10.493 --> 00:07:11.750
and this is what for
us as radio presenters,

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:13.160
it's the first time in our careers

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.400
that we can interact one on one

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:16.500
with people that listen to the show.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:18.560
So after the show, I
will get on to Instagram

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:20.450
and reply to nearly every
single Instagram message

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:21.330
that I get.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.360
We couldn't do that 10 years ago.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:24.193
This is a new...

00:07:24.193 --> 00:07:25.720
Even the radio is an old school platform.

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:26.960
It's now new school for us.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.120
- 100% and it's really
the origin of my career.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:30.780
When I was doing the wine show on YouTube

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.107
there wasn't that many people watching

00:07:32.107 --> 00:07:36.509
but every single person that
mentioned me or wine even

00:07:36.509 --> 00:07:39.320
on Twitter I engaged
with and I used to do it

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:41.800
for nine, 10 hours a day and it's really

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.400
how I built myself up.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:44.410
For everybody who's listening

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:46.223
who's trying to become an influencer--

00:07:46.223 --> 00:07:47.800
- [Woman] I was just gonna ask, yeah.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.603
- It's not just taking a
nice picture from the frame.

00:07:50.603 --> 00:07:54.200
It's also engaging with the
three people that say that's...

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:56.419
The audacity of somebody
who wants to become famous

00:07:56.419 --> 00:07:59.460
and they get five comments
and they don't have time

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:00.607
to say thank you?

00:08:00.607 --> 00:08:02.630
I'm like, you're not going anywhere.

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:04.160
- [Kris] I love that
reply to the comments.

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:08.400
In studio too, three people
listeners of this show.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:10.970
We put it out last week
to ask Gary a question.

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:12.227
- I love this.

00:08:12.227 --> 00:08:13.630
- [Kris] We got over 1,000 entries

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:17.140
and I'm gonna bring in
Jeremy, Kyle, and Emma.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:18.287
Please welcome to the studio.

00:08:18.287 --> 00:08:19.527
(cheering)

00:08:19.527 --> 00:08:20.360
There's Gary V guys.

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:23.320
- Hi, so nice to meet you. How are you?

00:08:23.320 --> 00:08:24.570
- How's it going?
- Hey brother, how are you?

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:25.580
I met this guy outside.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:26.865
He had Krispy Kreme and everything.

00:08:26.865 --> 00:08:27.885
(laughing)

00:08:27.885 --> 00:08:28.940
Good to see you.

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:29.830
How are you?

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:31.526
- [Kris] Good on you guys.

00:08:31.526 --> 00:08:32.359
Congratulations on being here.

00:08:32.359 --> 00:08:33.300
I'm so glad that A,
you listen to the show.

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:34.989
Thank you so much.

00:08:34.989 --> 00:08:35.822
I'm gonna bring Jeremy up first.

00:08:35.822 --> 00:08:37.769
Jeremy if you can come up
to the microphone over here.

00:08:37.769 --> 00:08:40.040
This is what a lot of people want.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.663
This one on one time with Gary V.

00:08:42.663 --> 00:08:44.560
This is a moment for you, right?

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.720
- So yesterday I was listening
to his podcast in the car

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:50.627
thinking I wonder if I met
him, what would I ask him?

00:08:50.627 --> 00:08:54.055
And now, 24 hours later
I'm sat in front of him

00:08:54.055 --> 00:08:54.888
or stood in front of him.

00:08:54.888 --> 00:08:56.270
So quick question.

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:59.475
We are actually launching an
online travel agency today.

00:08:59.475 --> 00:09:00.570
- Wow.

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.630
- After a year and a half of
work, we're launching today.

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:03.792
So the timing is unbelievable.

00:09:03.792 --> 00:09:04.625
- Karma.

00:09:04.625 --> 00:09:05.791
- [Kris] What's the name of it?

00:09:05.791 --> 00:09:08.650
- It's Kulu Tamam which means
everything's cool in Arabic.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:09.610
- [Kris] Could you spell it for me?

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:10.980
- K-U-L-U.

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.030
- [Kris] K-U-L-U, yep.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:14.410
- T-A-M-A-M.com.

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:15.243
- [Kris] Okay, cool.

00:09:15.243 --> 00:09:16.441
- That's a good start to the company.

00:09:16.441 --> 00:09:21.180
- So, as part of the launch
we're trying to build the brand

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:24.340
around an event and we've
signed with Emirates Holidays

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:26.500
to be a official travel agent for

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:27.629
the Asian Football Cup in January.

00:09:27.629 --> 00:09:28.700
- Amazing.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:31.269
- We're gonna run a competition
to win trips to the event.

00:09:31.269 --> 00:09:35.580
How do we boost that
engagement with the contests

00:09:35.580 --> 00:09:37.630
with a very, very small budget?

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:40.330
- To me it's all about Instagram DM.

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:42.780
It's about DMing people
on Instagram, letting...

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:45.842
Now, not just trying to get
them to build awareness for you.

00:09:45.842 --> 00:09:49.040
Asking them, hey, this
is what we're doing.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.200
What can I do for you?

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:51.421
This is what's important to me

00:09:51.421 --> 00:09:53.450
and just literally day by day,

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:54.450
we were just talking about it.

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:59.010
Day by day, in the trenches,
100, 1,000 people a day.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:00.495
I mean, in the beginning
when you're hungry

00:10:00.495 --> 00:10:03.400
to launch something it should be

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.834
hand to hand combat
but I think influencers

00:10:05.834 --> 00:10:10.590
are absolutely the underpriced
media of today's world

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:13.090
and especially in this
market when I look at it

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:17.450
and so just DMing 5,000 and
I know that sounds daunting

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:20.030
but it's just what you have
to do in the beginning.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:22.950
5,000 different people saying
we need awareness for this.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:24.035
What do you need?

00:10:24.035 --> 00:10:25.495
And then bartering.

00:10:25.495 --> 00:10:26.700
- [Kris] Love that advice.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:27.856
- Period.

00:10:27.856 --> 00:10:29.450
Good luck my friend.

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:31.540
- [Kris] It's Kulu Tamam.

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:32.869
Is it live now if I go to it?

00:10:32.869 --> 00:10:33.702
- It is live.

00:10:33.702 --> 00:10:36.710
- [Kris] K-U-L-U T-A-M-A-M.com.

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:37.543
